From 212fd15e62aeba2fbfb3bf31a9cb93a055aa49fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:49:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Home: WiFi status and a Scan WiFi button for Headunit
 Server

Headunit Server needs this unit on the phone's hotspot, and an Android 10
unit can sit a minute with that hotspot in range: the platform backs its
own reconnect scans off while nothing is connected. Once the unit joins,
the discovery loop finds the phone by itself, so one scan asked for by
hand is often all that is missing.

Headunit Server only (Manual and Auto), while the card is the WiFi one:
- beside the main button's icon, the network this unit is on, a band
  chip (2.4 / 5 / 6 GHz) and four signal bars with the percentage; not
  connected or off shows an amber dot, a "WiFi off" icon and a hint.
  Information only: it reacts to nothing.
- a Scan WiFi button beside the main button, the same size and pill
  shape: see-through white on the day card, the tile color at night. A
  tap asks Android for one scan (or opens the WiFi panel when WiFi is
  off) and turns an open ring until the results arrive; a long press
  opens the WiFi settings. It stands out while the unit is not on WiFi,
  and hides during a bring-up, the reconnect countdown and a session.

The main button, in every mode, becomes a pill led by an icon (a link
to connect, the arrow back to a session, refresh to search again), in
a medium weight, and on the day card a white with a breath of the
connection's color.

On a narrow card, one step per layout and held while the width holds:
Scan WiFi drops its label, then steps aside if the main button's label
would still be cut; the WiFi line takes the header spacer's share, its
name steps down a size and may take two lines, and the line under it
drops the bars before a hint takes two lines. HomeWifiStatusLayoutTest
lays the real home out on 1920x720, 1280x480, 1024x600, 1280x480 hdpi,
800x450, a portrait phone and a portrait tablet.

No connection logic changes. The rules are HomeWifiStatusPolicy, with
unit tests; strings in every locale.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
